# HG changeset patch
# User Betterbird <betterbird@betterbird.eu> and DeepSeek
# Date 1787993534 -7200
# Parent  5ce3fec1008ba2b59a21c3e6ea65d93c1e5979db
Feature: Linux systray. Implement support for Mate desktop.

  The current integrated copy of libayatana-appindicator
  implements only the StatusNotifierItem (SNI) D-Bus protocol. It
  registers via org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher on the session bus (
  NOTIFICATION_WATCHER_DBUS_ADDR in third_party/appindicator/dbus-shared.h)
  and only shows an icon if a watcher is present.

  Mate's mate-panel doesn't provide an SNI watcher — it only supports the
  legacy XEmbed system tray protocol. That's why Xfce (SNI plugin) and
  KDE (plasma has an SNI watcher) work, but Mate shows nothing:
  getConnectable() in ayatana-appindicator.c:508 just returns without
  doing anything when no watcher name owner exists.

  The previous bundled libappindicator (140 version) worked on Mate
  because it had an XEmbed fallback: when the watcher was absent,
  fallback_timer_expire() created a GtkStatusIcon (see the GtkStatusIcon/
  fallback/unfallback code). The Ayatana rewrite dropped that fallback.

  Fix:
  In nsMessengerUnixIntegration.cpp, detect Mate (via
  GetDesktopEnvironmentIdentifier()) and create a plain GtkStatusIcon
  instead of AppIndicator in that case.

